{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the distance from the origin to the plane passing through the points \\((-5,0,0)\\), \\((0,2,0)\\), and \\((0,0,-7)\\), we first need to determine the equation of the plane. The general form of the equation of a plane is given by:\n\n\\[ ax + by + cz = d. \\]\n\nSince the plane passes through the points \\((-5,0,0)\\), \\((0,2,0)\\), and \\((0,0,-7)\\), we can substitute these points into the plane equation to get a system of equations.\n\n1. Substituting \\((-5,0,0)\\) into the plane equation gives:\n\\[ -5a + 0b + 0c = d \\implies -5a = d \\implies d = -5a. \\]\n\n2. Substituting \\((0,2,0)\\) into the plane equation gives:\n\\[ 0a + 2b + 0c = d \\implies 2b = d \\implies d = 2b. \\]\n\n3. Substituting \\((0,0,-7)\\) into the plane equation gives:\n\\[ 0a + 0b - 7c = d \\implies -7c = d \\implies d = -7c. \\]\n\nFrom the above, we have three expressions for \\(d\\):\n\\[ d = -5a, \\quad d = 2b, \\quad d = -7c. \\]\n\n","prefix_end":885,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,6010,504,279,6238,311,279,11031,12299,1526,279,3501,1124,54934,20,11,15,11,15,10699,701,1124,1188,15,11,17,11,15,10699,701,323,1124,1188,15,11,15,4999,22,10699,701,582,1156,1184,311,8253,279,23606,315,279,11031,13,576,4586,1352,315,279,23606,315,264,11031,374,2661,553,1447,78045,3859,488,553,488,17988,284,294,13,1124,2533,12549,279,11031,16211,1526,279,3501,1124,54934,20,11,15,11,15,10699,701,1124,1188,15,11,17,11,15,10699,701,323,1124,1188,15,11,15,4999,22,10699,701,582,646,27679,1493,3501,1119,279,11031,23606,311,633,264,1849,315,37906,382,16,13,3719,3696,10607,1124,54934,20,11,15,11,15,10699,8,1119,279,11031,23606,6696,510,78045,481,20,64,488,220,15,65,488,220,15,66,284,294,1124,6383,550,481,20,64,284,294,1124,6383,550,294,284,481,20,64,13,1124,2533,17,13,3719,3696,10607,1124,1188,15,11,17,11,15,10699,8,1119,279,11031,2